Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::distinct_doorbells_never_collide`.

The defect: `doorbell` drops the factor of two in `index = 2 * queue_id + role`, so queue `q`'s
completion-head doorbell and queue `q + 1`'s submission-tail doorbell are the same register. A
head write then lands on a tail.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(doorbell(first_queue_id, first_role, doorbell_stride) != doorbell(second_queue_id, second_role, doorbell_stride))`.

